wq#1659 — [Unit] stanza changes for the 5 affected units. `litellm.service` and
`lumen-pgvector.service` are docker containers, not systemd units; `systemctl
daemon-reload` has never been able to resolve either name (FLEET_SERVICE_ATLAS.md
:68). Each unit already carries (or gets) Requires=docker.service so stopping
docker still stops it; this diff only fixes the ordering/wait lie.

--- a/etc/systemd/system/lumen-fleet-cerebras.service
+++ b/etc/systemd/system/lumen-fleet-cerebras.service
@@ [Unit]
-After=litellm.service
-Wants=litellm.service
+After=docker.service
 Requires=docker.service
@@ [Service]
+ExecStartPre=/home/lumen/bin/wait-for-port 127.0.0.1 4000 30

--- a/etc/systemd/system/lumen-fleet-mistral.service
+++ b/etc/systemd/system/lumen-fleet-mistral.service
@@ [Unit]
-After=litellm.service
-Wants=litellm.service
+After=docker.service
 Requires=docker.service
@@ [Service]
+ExecStartPre=/home/lumen/bin/wait-for-port 127.0.0.1 4000 30

--- a/etc/systemd/system/lumen-fleet-openrouter.service
+++ b/etc/systemd/system/lumen-fleet-openrouter.service
@@ [Unit]
-After=litellm.service
-Wants=litellm.service
+After=docker.service
 Requires=docker.service
@@ [Service]
+ExecStartPre=/home/lumen/bin/wait-for-port 127.0.0.1 4000 30

--- a/etc/systemd/system/lumen-convo-learn.service
+++ b/etc/systemd/system/lumen-convo-learn.service
@@ [Unit]
-After=litellm.service
-Wants=litellm.service
+After=docker.service
+Requires=docker.service
@@ [Service]
+ExecStartPre=/home/lumen/bin/wait-for-port 127.0.0.1 4000 30

--- a/etc/systemd/system/lumen-research-index.service
+++ b/etc/systemd/system/lumen-research-index.service
@@ [Unit]
-After=lumen-pgvector.service
+After=docker.service
+Requires=docker.service
@@ [Service]
+ExecStartPre=/home/lumen/bin/wait-for-port 127.0.0.1 5433 30

Notes:
- lumen-convo-learn and lumen-research-index did not previously declare
  Requires=docker.service (only the 3 fleet researchers did, per
  FLEET_SERVICE_ATLAS.md :55); adding it closes the same gap for them —
  stopping docker should stop anything that depends on a container it hosts.
- Port 4000 = litellm (FLEET_SERVICE_ATLAS.md :76; confirmed open via a live
  TCP probe, wq#1765 verify). Port 5433 = lumen-pgvector — NOT 5432. The
  original draft of this diff guessed 5432 ("standard postgres port
  convention") without checking the running container; wq#1765's verify pass
  probed 127.0.0.1 directly and found 5432 refused (something else — likely
  langfuse's own postgres — owns 5432) while 5433 is open. Applying the
  original 5432 hunk would have made every lumen-research-index.service run
  fail its ExecStartPre after the 30s timeout, turning today's benign
  ordering no-op into a real outage of the research-index job. Re-confirm
  with `python3 -c "import socket;s=socket.socket();s.settimeout(1);s.connect(('127.0.0.1',5433))"`
  (or equivalent) before applying, in case the container's port mapping has
  since changed.
- `@@ [Unit]` / `@@ [Service]` mark the section each hunk belongs in rather than
  claiming exact line numbers, since the live files are outside this worker's
  sandboxed directories (see RUNBOOK.md) and could not be read to anchor a
  byte-exact unified diff. Apply by section, not by line offset.
